technicalArbitrations:
What each phase proves while most tests cannot load:
- the ratchet: both type-error counts at or below the previous phase's, every recorded passing test still passing, and newly passing tests joining the record;
- the codemod's `--check` report: no leftover owned by the phase's skill;
- a named set of test files the phase must bring into the record once their imports load. The corpus replay (`tests/unit/effect4Corpus/replay.test.ts` and `wording.test.ts`) is due in the record by the end of phase-05 at the latest.
Behaviour is fully proven only at the end: phase-08 runs `pnpm check:full` itself, and the terminal gate runs it on phase-09. Loss accepted: phase-02 to phase-04 are judged mostly on falling counts and their own scope, not on running tests (spec q-green: ratchet).

detailedInstructions:
Step 4: run `pnpm exec tsx scripts/effect4-codemod/main.ts` once and keep its full output. It prints:
- the per-rule table (files, rewrites, reference lines);
- the files changed;
- the type-error counts of src and of the test suite, before and after;
- the `left to phases` list.
Then run `pnpm format`.

Scope: every leftover the codemod report puts under `effect4-schema` (Schema, ParseResult, JSONSchema, SchemaAST), in:
- src/**, except `src/schemas/history/**` and `src/schemas/publishedJsonSchema.ts`;
- tests/**, `tests/effect4Corpus/subjects.ts` included;
- scripts/**, except the scripts/schemas-*.ts files;
- site/**.
Also the method calls on schema values the report does not list (`.annotations(` → `.annotate(`). List the leftovers with `pnpm exec tsx scripts/effect4-codemod/main.ts --check`.

Port `src/schemas/refusal/adapter.ts` from ParseResult issues to Effect 4's SchemaIssue. It must produce the same refusal-model values (path, kind, expected label, actual value) for the same inputs:
- `missing` from MissingKey;
- `unexpected` from UnexpectedKey;
- `invalid-type` from InvalidType, naming a whole type by its kind;
- `invalid-value` and `filter` from the check failures, labelled from their data as before.
`src/schemas/refusal/render.ts` is not changed. After this phase, no module except the adapter imports SchemaIssue or reads an Effect issue, and no formatter matches Effect's message text (§5.15).

Migrate by the mapping table and the reference line each leftover cites:
- `Schema.pattern` → `Schema.isPattern`; `minLength`, `maxLength` and `minItems` → `isMinLength` and `isMaxLength`; the numeric filters → their `is*` checks;
- the other shapes of `Schema.filter` → `.check(Schema.makeFilter(p))` or `Schema.refine`;
- `Schema.optionalWith` with other options → `optional`, `optionalKey` or `withDecodingDefaultType`;
- `Schema.Schema.Any`, `All` and `AnyNoContext` → the v4 schema type the reference names;
- `ParseResult.ParseError` → the reference's `Schema.SchemaError`;
- the SchemaAST helpers used outside the generator.
Keep every annotation's meaning: identifiers, titles, descriptions, and the `jsonSchema` annotations on filters, which phase-08's generator reads.

Do not change:
- symbols owned by effect4-errors, effect4-services or effect4-core, even in a file you edit: `Either.*`, `Effect.catch*`, `Exit`, `Cause`, `Context`, `Layer` and the rest of `Effect` belong to phase-05 to phase-07;
- `src/schemas/history/**` (phase-04);
- `src/schemas/publishedJsonSchema.ts`, `packages/schemas/**` and the scripts/schemas-*.ts files (phase-08).

Before finishing:
- `--check` lists no leftover under `src/schemas/history/`;
- `pnpm codemod:effect4 --ratchet` passes;
- no `any`, silencing `as` or compatibility module was added.

Blockers first, everywhere outside `src/schemas/history/` (phase-04 finished it):
- `Either.flatMap`: the reference says `TODO: needs guidance`; resolve it against the installed `node_modules/effect` Result source;
- `Either.flip` → `Result.flip`;
- `Either.Left` → `Result.Failure`;
- `Either.getOrNull`: no reference entry; resolve against the installed source; if Result has no counterpart, use `Result.getOrElse(() => null)`;
- `Either.getOrUndefined` and `Either.getOrThrowWith` → their Result counterparts.
Then re-run `pnpm exec tsx scripts/effect4-codemod/main.ts`, so the 452 covered uses they held back are rewritten mechanically and not by hand, then `pnpm format`.

Migrate the rest of the topic:
- `Effect.catchAllCause` → `Effect.catchCause`;
- `Effect.catchTag` and `catchTags`, `Effect.orElse*`, `Effect.sandbox`;
- `Exit.isInterrupted` → `Exit.hasInterrupts`;
- `Cause.failureOption` → `Cause.findErrorOption`;
- `Data.TaggedError`.
Also the member accesses on the values these types give: `.left` and `.right` become `.failure` and `.success`.

Before finishing:
- `--check` lists no `effect4-errors` leftover;
- tsc reports no error at an errors-topic symbol;
- `pnpm codemod:effect4 --ratchet` passes.

The codemod already rewrote the ports' `Context.Tag` classes to `Context.Service`. Migrate:
- the reported services leftover (`Context.Tag.Service` → `Context.Service.Shape<T>`);
- every type error at a Context, Layer, ManagedRuntime, Runtime, FiberRef or Scope symbol, or at `Effect.Service`, `Effect.Tag` or the `Effect.provide*` family;
across src/ports, src/infra (layers), src/app, src/cli (the composition root and the ported command library's runtime), tests (test layers and fakes), scripts and site.

Before finishing:
- `--check` lists no `effect4-services` leftover;
- tsc reports no error at a services symbol;
- `pnpm codemod:effect4 --ratchet` passes.

Migrate the core leftovers from `docs/effect-4-mapping.md` §2, wherever the report lists them:
- `Effect.dieMessage` → `Effect.die` (reference 10045): keep the defect's message text identical wherever it can reach a user or a test;
- `Effect.zipRight` → `Effect.andThen`;
- `Array.isNonEmptyReadonlyArray` → `Array.isReadonlyArrayNonEmpty`;
- `Effect.async` → `Effect.callback`;
- `Effect.timeoutTo` → `Effect.timeoutOrElse` with `Effect.map`;
- `Effect.fork` → `Effect.forkChild`, checking with `forking.md` that the fiber's supervision is unchanged;
- `Effect.Effect.Context` → `Effect.Services`;
- `Predicate.isRecord` → `Predicate.isObject`, checking against the installed source that arrays and other values are classified as before.
Also every other type error at a symbol of Effect, Option, Data, Stream, Fiber or Duration that no other skill owns.

Before finishing:
- `--check` lists no `effect4-core` leftover;
- `pnpm codemod:effect4 --ratchet` passes;
- the remaining errors are only phase-08's.

Port the generator:
- `src/schemas/publishedJsonSchema.ts`: `JSONSchema.make`/`fromAST` → `Schema.toJsonSchemaDocument`, draft-07 target, per reference lines 11712 and 11700;
- `packages/schemas/build/jsonSchemas.ts`: `findJsonSchemaGaps` must still flag a refinement with no `jsonSchema` annotation, now an Effect 4 check, and must still not flag brand-only refinements, annotated filters or effect's built-ins;
- the SchemaAST helpers and annotation getters, per the mapping table.
The existing tests in `tests/unit/schemasPackage/jsonSchemas.test.ts` keep their expectations; only their Effect plumbing may change.

Build the equivalence judge in `packages/schemas/build/equivalence.ts`, as a pure module:
- given a released JSON Schema, a generated one and a list of documents, it validates every document against both with ajv (draft-07, already a devDependency);
- it returns the documents whose verdicts differ;
- `equivalent` is true when the two are equal as parsed JSON with annotations aside, or when the document list is not empty and no verdict differs. An empty list never proves equivalence.
The documents of a format are the `input` of every case in `tests/effect4Corpus/cases/formats/<id>.json`, read through the corpus's own loader in `tests/effect4Corpus/corpus.ts` if it exports one, else by parsing the case files. Never write to these files. For `record-manifest`, use the union of the three manifests' documents.

Add the in-phase tests:
- `tests/unit/schemasPackage/equivalence.test.ts` for the judge, with hand-built schema pairs: an empty document list is not equivalence, a disagreeing document is returned, annotations are ignored;
- `tests/unit/schemasPackage/shippedJson.test.ts`: the built `json/` equals `shipped-json.json` entry for entry, byte for byte, with one entry per shipped file;
- `tests/unit/schemasPackage/effect4Exports.test.ts`: every exported value that was a Schema at 0.36.0 passes the installed effect's `Schema.isSchema`.

Close the tree. Run:
- `pnpm exec tsx scripts/effect4-codemod/main.ts --check`: 0 files would change and no leftover listed (§5.3, §5.12);
- tsc on src and on `tsconfig.test.json`: zero errors;
- `pnpm check:full`, `pnpm build`, `pnpm site:build`, `pnpm deno:smoke` and `pnpm deno:smoke-binary`: all must pass.
A failure owned by an earlier topic is fixed at its symbol by that topic's skill and named in the handoff. Then run `pnpm codemod:effect4 --ratchet`.

docs/upgrading.md. Add an entry under the heading of the release that will carry the migration:
- the version in `package.json` (0.36.0) if that version is not yet released (check with `git show-ref --tags`);
- otherwise a new heading for the next minor, placed above it.
The entry says:
- phax runs on Effect 4, and commands, files and refusals are unchanged;
- @lbdremy/phax-schemas' exported Schema values (RegistrySchema, PhaxPlanSchema, …) are Effect 4 schemas, code composing them needs `effect ^4.1.2`, and code that only calls the parse functions changes nothing;
- the published JSON Schemas are unchanged, and phax checks the ones Effect 4 generates against them by the documents they accept (§5.21).

CLAUDE.md:
- `TypeScript 7 (native compiler) + Effect (v3)` becomes Effect 4;
- the conventions line that names `@effect/platform` no longer names it (the package is gone); it says to cross-check Effect APIs against `package.json`.

Skills, each checked against the current code before rewriting:
- `.claude/skills/state-machines/SKILL.md`: the Either sample (`Either<NewState, InvalidTransitionError>`, `import { Either }`, `Either.isLeft`, the `Left` wording) becomes Result, as `src/domain/state.ts` now returns it;
- `.claude/skills/infrastructure-adapters/SKILL.md`: `Context.Tag` becomes `Context.Service`, and the adapter table no longer names `@effect/platform/FileSystem` or `@effect/platform/Command`; it names what `src/infra/fs.ts`, `git.ts` and `shell.ts` actually use;
- `.claude/skills/observability/SKILL.md`: `Context.Tag` becomes `Context.Service`.
